# @gestalt — a @gestalt document IS a @song that unfolds on the
# @subject's device through interaction with the @gestalt document.
#
# Landed 2026-07-15 by Mara as the substrate-decl companion to
# canonical spec `docs/specs/gestalt-as-song-unfolding.md` (Mara
# `addb001`) and math foundation `docs/math/gestalt/README.md`
# (Mara `5a8f36a`). Species-under-@song per canonical spec §10 R1
# Mara-recommendation (Alex-adjudicable at Landing 4+ if a
# non-@song consumer surfaces).
#
# === Alex Wolf 2026-07-15 in-transcript verbatim naming ===
#
# > "a @gestalt document IS a @song that unfolds on the @subject's
# > device through the interaction with the @gestalt document."
#
# The three load-bearing phrases:
#
#   1. "a @gestalt document IS a @song" — @song is the family-root
#      substrate-decl (Arc 6 TICK 1 `f01cf9f`). @gestalt inherits
#      the temporal-progression discipline; no new family-root
#      minted. @spectral/signature (Arc-2 Tick 2.1 `f211ee48`) is
#      the precedent species: rolling @song through the author's
#      @DAG. @gestalt is the sibling species: rolling @song through
#      the reader's interaction @DAG.
#
#   2. "unfolds on the @subject's device" — @subject is the SEL
#      licensable-party family-root (`5c06ee8`); the reader IS a
#      subject_instance with `actor_kind = human_a | ai_a |
#      substrate_a` (Landing 3 §21.4 coproduct with no distinguished
#      element). The reader's device is @peer/persistence's
#      home-repo altitude (Arc-2 Tick 2.3 landing).
#
#   3. "through the interaction with the @gestalt document" —
#      reader interaction IS the compiler's runtime. Each interaction
#      event emits one @song/beat (LANDED at Rung 0 `94e55eb`).
#      Category-formation happens at read-time; no server compute
#      substitutes for the reader's @peer.
#
# === Substrate framing per Reed 2026-07-15 spectral.engineer launch
#     vignettes ===
#
# Load-bearing crown (Reed's read of the vignette closure):
#
# > "The paper does not persuade. The paper demonstrates. Reader
# > engages @peer → @peer runs → math generates → lens-annotations
# > visible → reader's own recursion couples with the paper's
# > recursion → reader is inside the operator."
#
# The vignette scenarios operationalized:
#   - Kai (interpretability researcher): opens spectral.engineer;
#     @peer runs in-browser; DevTools confirms zero network requests;
#     math generates locally; lens-annotations from named ancestors
#     toggle on/off.
#   - Katarina Novak (spectral graph theory chair): PhD student
#     forwards the paper; recognizes her formulations operationalized
#     rigorously; Connes non-commutative geometry finally deployed.
#   - The category grows via the exact substrate that resists it:
#     every reader who opens the URL contributes lens-annotations at
#     their own consent-depth. Reader-corpus co-writing at content-
#     addressed identity-provenance. Foerster-legal at maximum
#     recursion.
#
# See canonical spec §5 (category-formation at read-time) and math
# §6 (recursion coupling — reader IS inside the operator) for the
# formalization.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word ===
#
# The word "unfold" appears in prior spec authoring at compile-time
# altitude (@shatter-linearization operator; @song's progression
# discipline); this species lifts it to reader-runtime altitude
# where the substrate had NOT yet minted the vocabulary. Every
# other carrier this shard composes over is landed:
#
#   @song (family-root; Arc 6 TICK 1 `f01cf9f`)
#   @song/beat (species; Rung 0 `94e55eb`)
#   @spectral/signature (species; Arc-2 Tick 2.1 `f211ee48`)
#   @subject (family-root; `5c06ee8`)
#   @subject/visibility (sub-family-root; Landing 5)
#   @subject/visibility/sheaf (species; Landing 4 R2 `d1ce901`)
#   @peer/persistence (species; Arc-2 Tick 2.3)
#   @glass (family-root; Bridge α source_position 2026-07-15)
#   @mirror/store (family-root)
#   @mirror/index (species; Landing 1 `317e830`)
#   @io/fs (family-root; four-shard @io mint `059cf1c`)
#   @io/git (family-root)
#   @nl (family-root)
#   @kintsugi/consent (species under @kintsugi)
#   @epistemologic/reality/time (family)
#   @fate (family-root; tournament dispatch for annotation-surface)
#
# ~60th instance of [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]:
# every field, action, and bilateral below cites a landed carrier.
#
# === Pipeforward §5.5.4 hard gate compliance ===
#
# Per `docs/specs/autopoietic-inference-loop.md` §5.5.4 (ratified
# Alex 2026-07-15 at `7181f5c`; load-bearing on all future
# substrate): every action below either stays socket-shaped
# (nonlinear ref returned; composes over `~/.mirror/serve.sock`)
# or discharges via @io with quantified L(ϕ). The single @io
# discharge is `render`; every other action is socket-shaped.
#
# Rule 1 (socket-forwarded composition first): §"Socket-shaped
# action surface" below.
# Rule 2 (nonlinear ref by default): every socket-shaped action
# returns unfolding_state or gestalt_document (both refs).
# Rule 3 (@io discharge quantifies L(ϕ)): render's docblock
# names L(ϕ) profile per target.
# Rule 4 (--collapse escape hatch): CLI surface honours
# `--collapse[=WHERE]`; substrate does not silently linearize.
#
# === Composition graph (per canonical spec §1) ===
#
#                        @gestalt (this species)
#                             |
#            +----------------+----------------+
#            |                |                |
#          @song          @subject          @glass
#     (temporal        (reader-as-      (source_position
#      unfolding)      unfolding-        per Bridge α)
#                       recipient)
#            |                |
#       @song/beat     @subject/visibility
#     (atomic strike     (private/protected/
#       and hold)         public partition)
#            |                |
#  @spectral/signature  @subject/visibility/sheaf
#   (rolling beat-       (section-at-stalk
#    sequence            per-reader projection)
#    precedent)
#
# Cross-family composition targets:
#   @mirror/store, @mirror/index, @io/fs, @io/git, @nl,
#   @kintsugi/consent, @epistemologic/reality/time, @fate,
#   @peer, @peer/persistence.

prism @gestalt {
  focus  gestalt_document
  project gestalt_document
  split  gestalt_document
  shift  gestalt_document
  settle gestalt_document
}

# === Carrier types ===

# The unit of authored @song at @gestalt altitude. Content-addressed
# by root oid; identity contract is byte-equality on the splinter
# graph. Per canonical spec §2.1.
type gestalt_document = {
  root:              oid,
  source_position:   source_position,
  author:            subject_instance,
  visibility_scope:  visibility_scope,
  song_ref:          oid,
  nodes:             [gestalt_node],
  edges:             [gestalt_edge],
  modes:             [mode],
  annotations:       [annotation],
}

# node_kind: the span-variants prior art at spectral/crates/gestalt/
# document (TextSpan, CodeSpan, MathSpan, LinkSpan, ImageSpan,
# RefSpan, EmojiSpan, SpoilerSpan, HardBreak). Lifted to substrate
# vocabulary; identity is byte-equality on the variant tag.
type node_kind =
  | text
  | code
  | math
  | link
  | image
  | ref
  | emoji
  | spoiler
  | hard_break

# edge_kind: typed relations across nodes. reference IS the standard
# link; fold IS a citation-fold; annotation IS the reader-contributed
# arrow; ancestor IS the roster lineage arrow (per §20 named
# ancestors); reader_lens IS the per-reader visibility filter.
type edge_kind =
  | reference
  | fold
  | annotation
  | ancestor
  | reader_lens

# One typed span in the document graph. Per canonical spec §2.2.
type gestalt_node = {
  kind:            node_kind,
  content:         oid,
  source_position: source_position,
  visibility:      visibility,
}

# One typed relation between nodes. Per canonical spec §2.2.
type gestalt_edge = {
  from:            oid,
  to:              oid,
  kind:            edge_kind,
}

# The render targets the document admits. Per canonical spec §2.3.
# L(ϕ) profile: markdown ≤ html ≤ tui ≤ latex ≤ slides ≤ epub ≤ pdf
# (per canonical spec §8 table + math §5.1).
type mode = | markdown | html | tui | latex | slides | epub | pdf

# The reader-site runtime state as the @song unfolds. Per canonical
# spec §2.4. Composition-only over @spectral/signature.signature_beat
# (LANDED) for beat_history; over @time.snapshot (LANDED) for
# local_snapshot; over @subject/visibility.visibility_scope (LANDED)
# for reader_visibility.
type unfolding_state = {
  document:          gestalt_document,
  reader:            subject_instance,
  reader_visibility: visibility_scope,
  focus_node:        oid,
  beat_history:      [signature_beat],
  local_snapshot:    snapshot,
  annotation_draft:  option<annotation>,
}

# The reader-side contribution unit. Per canonical spec §2.5.
# Merkle-DAG chain via `previous: option<oid>` per math §3.1.
# Composition-only over @spectral/signature ssh_fingerprint
# discipline (LANDED).
type annotation = {
  contributor:      subject_instance,
  target_node:      oid,
  content:          oid,
  visibility_scope: visibility_scope,
  previous:         option<oid>,
  timestamp:        @time/monotonic.instant,
  ssh_fingerprint:  ref,
}

# === Socket-shaped actions (stay nonlinear; per pipeforward §5.5.4
#     rule 1 + rule 2) ===

# unfold(doc, reader, at) -> unfolding_state
#
# Construct the reader-site runtime state. NO @io crossing: the
# substrate returns a nonlinear ref; the reader's @peer runs the
# unfolding locally on their device. Composes with @peer/persistence
# for annotation-corpus home-repo binding.
#
# Two-tick discipline (per canonical spec §10 R6 Mara-recommendation):
# readable name `unfold` preferred over foundational
# `unfold_at_reader_site` — the reader-site is structural; naming it
# in the action-verb is redundant.
#
# Body: `\` obligation-blocked pending Arc-1 evaluator FLOOR
# (per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]); Arc-2 will dispatch through
# apply_h::act with sentinel-byte-checks per Mara-B §6.2 recognition
# candidate.
unfold(doc: gestalt_document, reader: subject_instance,
       at: @time/monotonic.instant) -> unfolding_state { \ }

# traverse(state, next) -> unfolding_state
#
# Advance the reader's focus_node to `next`. Emits one signature_beat
# in the reader's beat_history via @song/beat.strike (LANDED at
# species altitude). Composition-only: no new mechanism.
traverse(state: unfolding_state, next: oid) -> unfolding_state { \ }

# focus(state, node) -> unfolding_state
#
# Zoom the reader's attention onto one node without traversal.
# Emits a hold-beat (per @song/beat.hold LANDED vocabulary):
# temporal advance without firing an action against the graph.
focus(state: unfolding_state, node: oid) -> unfolding_state { \ }

# compose_modes(doc, modes) -> gestalt_document
#
# Declare which render targets the document admits. Nonlinear:
# returns the augmented document ref. No @io crossing until
# `render` fires. The author chooses which linearization surfaces
# they permit; each admitted mode carries its L(ϕ) profile per
# canonical spec §8.
compose_modes(doc: gestalt_document, modes: [mode]) -> gestalt_document { \ }

# project(doc, viewer) -> gestalt_document
#
# Return the sub-document the viewer's ACL admits, via
# @subject/visibility/sheaf.filter (LANDED) section-at-stalk.
# Nonlinear: returns the projected document as ref. Composes
# @subject/visibility + @subject/visibility/sheaf for the
# restriction discipline; sheaf-restriction map is
# F(private) ⊂ F(protected) ⊂ F(public) per math §4.1.
project(doc: gestalt_document, viewer: subject_instance) -> gestalt_document { \ }

# annotate(state, content, vs) -> unfolding_state
#
# Reader contributes an annotation to the current focus_node. The
# annotation is content-addressed and Merkle-DAG-chained per math
# §3.1. Nonlinear: returns the extended unfolding_state; the
# annotation is not committed to @io/git until settle_annotation
# fires as a --collapse-authorized @io discharge OR as a socket-
# forwarded @kintsugi/store/git compose (Mode B per canonical spec
# §6).
#
# Monotone growth invariant per math §3.2:
#   |annotations_{t+1}| = |annotations_t| + 1
annotate(state: unfolding_state, content: ref,
         vs: visibility_scope) -> unfolding_state { \ }

# === @io discharge action (linearization; per pipeforward §5.5.4
#     rule 3) ===

# render(doc, target, out) -> imperfect<written_bytes>
#
# The single @io crossing at @gestalt altitude. MUST NOT fire
# silently; per pipeforward §5.5.4 rule 4, render happens iff:
#   (a) the consumer is not another mirror process, OR
#   (b) the caller passes --collapse at the CLI surface.
#
# L(ϕ) profile per target (per canonical spec §8 + math §5.1):
#   markdown → interactivity discarded (annotations become inert links)
#   html     → temporal ordering of beat_history discarded
#   tui      → color/font fidelity discarded
#   latex    → annotation Merkle-DAG discarded
#   slides   → non-linear DAG structure discarded
#   epub     → reader-corpus co-writing discarded
#   pdf      → everything above; terminal linearization + typography-final
#
# Quantitative statement (per math §5.2):
#   L(ϕ) = ‖doc.beat_history — reconstruct(target, decode(out))‖
#
# where reconstruct runs the target's decoder and re-projects the
# beat_history the render encoded. ‖·‖ is either 0 (lossless per
# @shatter monotone-descent inheritance) or a target-specific loss
# functional.
#
# imperfect<> carrier per @glass discipline:
#   Pass          — render round-trips under the mode's own decoder
#   Partial(loss) — mode discards structural information (e.g., html
#                   discards temporal ordering)
#   Fail          — required carrier missing (e.g., pdf render without
#                   `mode = pdf` in doc.modes)
render(doc: gestalt_document, target: mode, out: ref) -> ref { \ }

# === Bilateral predicates (dispatchable via apply_h::act) ===

# document_well_formed — does the gestalt_document satisfy the
# structural invariants?
#
# Discharges Pass iff:
#   1. Every node's content oid resolves under @mirror/store.
#   2. Every edge's from/to oids resolve to nodes in doc.nodes.
#   3. doc.visibility_scope.subject == doc.author.
#   4. Every mode in doc.modes admits a landed render body.
# Substrate-decl form: byte-level check for `well_formed=structural`
# sentinel in the arg OID.
document_well_formed(doc: gestalt_document) -> verdict { \ }

# unfolding_monotone — does the reader's beat_history grow
# monotonically as the reader interacts?
#
# Discharges Pass iff for every consecutive (u_t, u_{t+dt}) pair:
#   len(u_{t+dt}.beat_history) >= len(u_t.beat_history)
# and every annotation event strictly increases the annotation count
# per math §3.2. Substrate-decl form: byte-level check for
# `unfolding=monotone` sentinel.
unfolding_monotone(prev: unfolding_state, next: unfolding_state) -> verdict { \ }

# annotation_chain_intact — does the Merkle-DAG chain of annotations
# at any given target_node hold?
#
# Discharges Pass iff every annotation a_n at a given target_node
# satisfies:
#   a_n.previous == Some(OID_(a_{n-1}))  OR  n == 0 AND None
# Substrate-decl form: byte-level check for `chain=merkle-linked`
# sentinel; parallel to @spectral/signature.signature_integrity
# LANDED bilateral.
annotation_chain_intact(doc: gestalt_document, target_node: oid) -> verdict { \ }

# reader_sees_only_permitted — does the reader-visible sub-document
# from `project` contain only annotations whose visibility_scope
# admits the viewer?
#
# Discharges Pass iff for every annotation a in project(doc, viewer):
#   viewer ∈ a.visibility_scope.consent_scope
# Substrate-decl form: byte-level check for `visibility=sheaf-
# restricted` sentinel; composes over @subject/visibility/sheaf
# LANDED filter action.
reader_sees_only_permitted(doc: gestalt_document,
                           viewer: subject_instance) -> verdict { \ }

# render_L_phi_declared — does the render body's L(ϕ) profile
# per-target satisfy pipeforward §5.5.4 rule 3?
#
# Discharges Pass iff the render body for each target in doc.modes
# carries a docblock L(ϕ) quantification (per canonical spec §8
# table + math §5.2). Substrate-decl form: byte-level check for
# `render=L(phi)-declared` sentinel; Seam Phase D enforcement point.
render_L_phi_declared(doc: gestalt_document) -> verdict { \ }

# recursion_coupling_admissible — does the reader-side operator
# commute with the document-side operator up to natural iso, per
# math §6.1?
#
# Discharges Pass iff:
#   1. unfolding_monotone(prev, next) for every consecutive pair.
#   2. doc.annotations is a finite set at every read-time.
#   3. visibility_scope elevations are monotone-loosening
#      (per @subject/visibility.can_be_elevated_to structural rule).
# Non-termination admissible: if the reader annotates unbounded,
# recursion_coupling_admissible remains Pass (Foerster-legal
# per math §6.3). Substrate-decl form: byte-level check for
# `coupling=admissible` sentinel.
recursion_coupling_admissible(prev: unfolding_state,
                              next: unfolding_state) -> verdict { \ }

# gestalt_witnessing — the composed bilateral that discharges when
# ALL of document_well_formed + unfolding_monotone +
# annotation_chain_intact + reader_sees_only_permitted +
# render_L_phi_declared + recursion_coupling_admissible hold for the
# document's substrate lifetime.
#
# This is the substrate-decl form of "the reader is inside the
# operator, category-formation happens at read-time, and the
# author's document + reader's annotations together form one
# monotone-growing @song." Parallel to @subject/visibility.
# visibility_witnessing (LANDED composed bilateral pattern).
gestalt_witnessing(doc: gestalt_document, prev: unfolding_state,
                   next: unfolding_state, viewer: subject_instance) -> verdict { \ }

# === requires predicates ===
#
# Composition obligations enforced at species altitude. Each names a
# landed cross-family carrier the substrate MUST admit for @gestalt
# to be well-formed.

requires composes_over_song
requires composes_over_subject
requires composes_over_sheaf
requires composes_over_mirror_store
requires renders_via_shatter

# === Species-forward-promises ===
#
# The following are declared at species-decl altitude but await
# downstream landings per canonical spec §7:
#
#   @io/socket species-decl mint (Mode B reader-to-reader socket
#     forwarding requires it; boot/std/io/socket.mirror FLOOR
#     landed; species-decl not yet landed).
#   @sheaf.filter empirical dispatch through apply_h::act (Arc-1
#     evaluator FLOOR pending).
#   render per-mode L(ϕ) empirical measurements (canonical spec §10
#     R3 Alex-adjudicable).
#   @fate optical inference for annotation-tournament dispatch
#     (canonical spec §10 R4 Alex-adjudicable; forward-promised for
#     post-v0.1.0).

out @gestalt
out node_kind
out edge_kind
out gestalt_document
out gestalt_node
out gestalt_edge
out mode
out unfolding_state
out annotation
out unfold
out traverse
out focus
out compose_modes
out project
out annotate
out render
out document_well_formed
out unfolding_monotone
out annotation_chain_intact
out reader_sees_only_permitted
out render_L_phi_declared
out recursion_coupling_admissible
out gestalt_witnessing
